thor":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Bitcoin Wealth","alternateName":["BW","Bitcoin Wealth Vow Unity"],"description":"A Bitcoin matrix programme run by a smart contract on BNB Smart Chain: members enter once with 0.001 BTC (as BTCB) and payments move wallet to wallet."},"width":1280,"height":720,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/","transcript":"Thandi: Leo, you said the book is open. But how do I actually read it? I'm not a computer person! Leo: You don't need to be. If you can track a parcel, you can do this. Welcome back, family. Today: 4 steps on BscScan, on your phone. Leo: BscScan is a block explorer: a public window into BNB Smart Chain. You know a parcel's tracking number? You type it in, and you see every stop the parcel made. Here, you type in the contract's address, and you see every payment it ever made. Where the picture stops: it shows wallet addresses, never people's names. Thandi: Okay, step one. Where do I find the contract's address? Leo: On the guide's Check It Yourself page. Copy it from there. Then type bscscan.com yourself. Never tap a BscScan link someone sends you: fake sites copy it to steal wallets. Paste the address, and check the first and the last characters match. Thandi: I'm in! What am I looking at? Leo: This is the contract's own page. The Transactions tab lists every activation since April 2026, newest on top: over 41,000 member IDs by mid November. Each row is one transaction, with the time it happened. Thandi: Can I open one? Leo: Step 2. Tap any transaction. Here's a real one, from the 24th of November. Scroll to ERC-20 Tokens Transferred. 0.001 BTCB goes into the contract, and in the same transaction, 0.001 BTCB goes straight out to another member's own wallet. Nobody pressed a button. The program did it. Thandi: So the money doesn't sit there. It goes straight on! I can see it! Leo: Step 3: Token Holdings. The contract does hold some BTCB: on the 24th of November, about 0.54. That's where the Royal Pool waits for its monthly payout. Leo: Step 4: your own wallet. Once you're a member, paste your own wallet address into BscScan, the same way. You'll see your own activation, and every payment in and out of your wallet, each with the time it happened. Nobody has to tell you. You see it for yourself. Thandi: Let me say it back. I type BscScan myself. Transactions: every activation. Thandi: One transaction: the payment goes straight on. Thandi: Token Holdings: the Royal Pool. And my own wallet: every payment, in and out. Leo: That's it! You've got it. And that's how we learn best: by teaching others. Leo: This is education, not financial advice. So take your time, and do your own research. Thandi: What's next, Leo? Leo: Next: your very own Bitcoin Wealth marketing website, with your own link. Leo: Already sharing Bitcoin Wealth with people? Picture your own website: bitcoinwealthpays.com/yourname. Like bitcoinwealthpays.com/zizi. This whole guide, every tutorial and every explainer, with MTG's branding taken off, and your name, your WhatsApp and your socials on it. Every Join button carries your own referral link, so everyone who signs up there joins your team. Your website shares the guide for you, day and night. Thandi: My own website, with my own link? I want that! Leo: And when you're ready to start, every step is at mtgtribe.com/bw. Thandi: See you there! Leo: If you want to go fast, go alone. If you want to go far, go together. Leo: Thank you for watching. Take good care of yourself, and of the people you love. We can't wait to welcome you. Goodbye for now.","hasPart":[{"@type":"Clip","name":"The book is open, but how do I read it?","startOffset":0,"endOffset":19,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=0"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"What BscScan is: a block explorer","startOffset":19,"endOffset":40,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=19"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Step 1: open the contract on BscScan","startOffset":40,"endOffset":81,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=40"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Step 2: open one transaction","startOffset":81,"endOffset":114,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=81"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Step 3: Token Holdings","startOffset":114,"endOffset":127,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=114"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Step 4: your own wallet","startOffset":127,"endOffset":144,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=127"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Thandi says it back","startOffset":144,"endOffset":176,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=144"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Next: your own Bitcoin Wealth website","startOffset":176,"endOffset":219,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=176"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Every step, and goodbye","startOffset":219,"endOffset":262,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/?t=219"}],"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/#video-e5","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/explainers/check-it-yourself-on-bscscan-video/#webpage"}}]}</script>
