"publisher":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Bitcoin Wealth","alternateName":["BW","Bitcoin Wealth Vow Unity"],"description":"A Bitcoin matrix programme run by a smart contract on BNB Smart Chain: members enter once with 0.001 BTC (as BTCB) and payments move wallet to wallet."},"width":720,"height":1280,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/buy-bnb-send-to-safepal/","transcript":"Hi, my name is MTG, Your Digital Architect. Thank you for taking the time to watch this video. In this video, I'll show you how to send rand from your bank to VALR, buy BNB with it, and send that BNB to your SafePal wallet. Using Binance instead? The steps are very similar. Take your time. You can pause any step and follow along with me. First, let's get your rand into VALR! Open the VALR app and tap Assets, at the bottom right. Under Cash and stablecoins, tap Rand. Can't see it? Tap Search and type rand. Your rand wallet has three buttons: Buy and sell, Deposit and Withdraw. Tap Deposit. Keep Fiat deposit, with ZAR as the currency, and tap the arrow next to Method. Choose EFT, a normal transfer from your bank. That's the one I recommend. Read these notes. VALR only accepts EFT payments from a bank account in your own name. No cash and no cheques. Don't deposit the same amount more than once a day. And a deposit can take up to 2 business days to reflect. Below that are VALR's bank details at Standard Bank. And at the bottom, your reference number. Every VALR customer has their own reference. It's how VALR knows the money is yours. Look here, this one's important. Copy the details, then open your banking app. I use FNB. Your bank may hide some screens while you record, so parts of my screen go dark. That's normal. Tap Pay, then Pay again. The first time, choose Once-off payment, paste VALR's details, and save VALR as a recipient, so next time there's nothing to copy. I saved it already, so I just pick VALR Crypto Exchange. How much? The only slot you ever pay for is slot 1: 0.001 Bitcoin. On 15 November 2026, Bitcoin was about $65,300 on CoinGecko, so 0.001 was about $65. To cover the fees, I send about $76, R1,300. Now the most important part. Type your reference exactly as VALR shows it, and check the account number. FNB asks for the reference twice. One wrong letter, and your money can't find your VALR account. That reference number is everything! Tick Real-time payment, so the money arrives in minutes, not days. Your bank may charge a small fee for it. Then tap Pay. Check the Please confirm screen: VALR Crypto Exchange, Standard Bank, the amount and your reference. Tap Confirm, then Finish. Back in VALR, tap Back, then Assets. There it is. My rand arrived within minutes, on a Sunday. Now, let's buy BNB! Tap Trade, in the middle at the bottom, then Buy and sell. Keep Buy. It says buy BTC, pay with ZAR. Tap the arrow next to BTC and choose BNB. Tap Max to use all your rand, then Review order. Check it, and swipe to confirm. Order completed. Tap View BNB wallet. Almost there! Tap Withdraw. VALR needs your SafePal address. Open SafePal, tap Receive, choose BNB, BEP20, and tap Copy. Back in VALR, paste it. Check that the network says Binance Smart Chain, the same as BNB Smart Chain. Tap Use all, then Next. Double check this. VALR asks who you're sending to. Choose Individual, and type your own name, because it's your own wallet. Under Wallet, choose Self-hosted wallet. Tick the box, and tap Next. Self-hosted means your own wallet. Check the address. The first few and the last few characters must match your SafePal address. Then tap Confirm withdrawal. VALR emails you a link to approve it. Open the email, tap Authorise transaction, and enter the code from your authenticator app. Withdrawal request received. Tap Close. Open SafePal and refresh. My BNB arrived: about $79 worth, a little more than 0.001 Bitcoin. If yours arrived too, comment DONE. No VALR or Binance account yet? Tap the buttons below this video to open one. I use both. It's smart to have a backup, just like having more than one income stream. Builders, a website like this one, with your own name and your links, does the explaining for you. BW stands for Bitcoin Wealth, and you can order yours at mtgtribe.com/bwcopy. We meet live on Zoom 5 evenings a week, in 4 languages. Ask the person who invited you to add you to the WhatsApp group, or tap the WhatsApp button below this video. Let's recap what we covered in this video. We sent rand from our bank to VALR, with our own reference. We bought BNB with it. And we sent the BNB to SafePal, on BNB Smart Chain. In the next video, part 3, I'll show you how to swap your BNB for BTCB, sign up with the link of the person who invited you, and activate slot 1. And remember: everyone needs their own copy. mtgtribe.com/bwcopy. Everything I showed you, plus my links, is at mtgtribe.com/bw. This video is for every team, so feel free to share it. Save this video, so it's here when you need it. Share it with someone who's ready to start. We learn best when we teach others. It pays to pay attention, and take action. Quick reminder: none of this is financial advice. Always do your own research. Thank you for tuning in, and for every like, share, and comment. Your support means everything. And thank yourself for taking massive action today to change your future! I wish you nothing but the best, because YOU are the best. I'm MTG, Your Digital Architect. See you on the next one. Let's Get This Crypto! 💪","hasPart":[{"@type":"Clip","name":"Deposit rand into VALR","startOffset":22,"endOffset":160,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/buy-bnb-send-to-safepal/?t=22"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Buy BNB","startOffset":160,"endOffset":185,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/buy-bnb-send-to-safepal/?t=160"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Send your BNB to SafePal","startOffset":185,"endOffset":285,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/buy-bnb-send-to-sa