 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#site","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/","name":"Bitcoin Wealth Guide by MTG","alternateName":["Bitcoin Wealth Guide","MTG Bitcoin Wealth","mtgtribe.com/bw"],"description":"Independent, plain-English Bitcoin Wealth education by MTG: how it works, how to join safely, free tools, and how to check every payment on the blockchain.","inLanguage":"en-ZA","publisher":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"author":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"}},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg","name":"MTG","alternateName":["MusaTheGiant","Musa the Giant"],"jobTitle":"Your Digital Architect","description":"MTG, Your Digital Architect: creator of independent, plain-English crypto education, videos and free tools, and host of the MTG TRIBE community.","url":"https://www.musathegiant.com","sameAs":["https://www.musathegiant.com","https://www.tiktok.com/@joinmtgtribe","https://www.youtube.com/@mtgtribe","https://www.facebook.com/mtgtribe","https://t.me/mtgtribe"],"knowsAbout":["Bitcoin","Bitcoin Wealth","BTCB","Web3 wallets","SafePal","BNB Smart Chain","Crypto safety","Affiliate marketing"]},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#webpage","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/","name":"How to set up SafePal for Bitcoin Wealth: Tutorial 1 | MTG","description":"Video and written steps: download SafePal from the official site, create your wallet, back it up two ways and keep only BNB, USDT and BTCB.","inLanguage":"en-ZA","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#site"},"author":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Bitcoin Wealth","alternateName":["BW","Bitcoin Wealth Vow Unity"],"description":"A Bitcoin matrix programme run by a smart contract on BNB Smart Chain: members enter once with 0.001 BTC (as BTCB) and payments move wallet to wallet."},"isAccessibleForFree":true,"datePublished":"2026-11-14","dateModified":"2026-11-22","breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#breadcrumb"},"video":[{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#video-t1"}],"hasPart":[{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#howto"}],"primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/img/bitcoin-wealth-safepal-wallet-setup-preview.jpg?v=973facb4","width":1200,"height":630}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Bitcoin Wealth guide","item":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Dashboard","item":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Tutorial Videos","item":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":4,"name":"Tutorial 1: Set up SafePal","item":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/"}],"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"VideoObject","name":"How to set up a SafePal wallet for Bitcoin Wealth (Tutorial 1)","description":"Download SafePal from the official site, create a wallet, back it up two ways, and keep only BNB, USDT and BTCB.","thumbnailUrl":["https://mtgtribe.com/bw/img/bitcoin-wealth-tutorial-1-safepal-wallet-setup-wide.webp","https://mtgtribe.com/bw/img/bitcoin-wealth-tutorial-1-safepal-wallet-setup.webp"],"uploadDate":"2026-11-14T00:00:00+02:00","duration":"PT7M25S","contentUrl":"https://media.bitcoinwealthpays.com/videos/bitcoin-wealth-tutorial-1-safepal-wallet-setup.mp4","encodingFormat":"video/mp4","inLanguage":"en-ZA","isFamilyFriendly":true,"isAccessibleForFree":true,"author":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/#mtg"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Bitcoin Wealth","alternateName":["BW","Bitcoin Wealth Vow Unity"],"description":"A Bitcoin matrix programme run by a smart contract on BNB Smart Chain: members enter once with 0.001 BTC (as BTCB) and payments move wallet to wallet."},"width":720,"height":1280,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/","transcript":"Hi, my name is MTG, Your Digital Architect. Thank you for taking the time to watch this video. In this video, I'll show you how to set up your SafePal wallet for Bitcoin Wealth, step by step, on your phone. We'll download the official app, create a brand new wallet, and back it up two ways. Then we'll clean it up, so it shows only the three coins you need. And I'll show you what it costs to get started. Take your time. You can pause any step and follow along with me. Why a Web3 wallet? A Web3 wallet is an app where you hold your own crypto, with your own keys. No bank, no company and no admin holds it for you. Bitcoin Wealth pays wallet to wallet, straight into yours. In this video, we use SafePal. Other Web3 wallets, like MetaMask, work too. First, download the official app. Only from safepal.com. Open your browser and go to safepal.com, the official website. Always download apps from the official website, never from a link someone sends you. Scroll down, and tap Download App. On Android, tap Get it on Google Play. On iPhone, tap App Store. Before you install, check two things: the developer, SafePal Wallet, and more than 5 million downloads. That's how you know it's the real app. Then tap Install. If Google Play shows you an offer, tap Decline offer. Stay focused. When it's done, tap Open. Tap Create New Wallet. We're making a brand new wallet, just for Bitcoin Wealth. Create a 6-digit password, then type it again to confirm. It unlocks SafePal on this phone. Your wallet is ready. Read this with me: Secure your wallet by saving your mnemonic phrase. This unique set of words is your only key to access your funds. SafePal cannot store or recover it for you. Your mnemonic phrase is your 12 secret recovery words. Whoever has them, has your wallet. This is the most important part of this video, so save it now. It'll be here when you do it yourself. Now back it up, two ways. Never skip this. Tap Back Up Now. Never skip this. There are two ways to back up, and we'll do both. First, Back up to Google Drive. Choose your Google account, then enter your 6-digit password. Now create a backup password. Easy for you to remember, hard for anyone to guess: at least 8 characters, with letters and numbers. Only tap the eye if nobody is around you. SafePal can't reset this password, so write it down. Your backup file is encrypted on your phone. Encrypted means locked with your password, so nobody can read it without it. Then it goes to your Google Drive. SafePal doesn't keep a copy. Tap Next. Read these before you tick them. The backup password is not your wallet password. It only restores your wallet from cloud storage, which means your Google Drive, online. It can't be changed or recovered. If you lose it, you can't restore from Google Drive. Tick all three, and tap Start Backup. Done. Your first backup is safe. Now give your wallet a clear name. Tap the wallet name at the top, then the three dots next to your wallet, and the pencil. Type Bitcoin Wealth, and tap Confirm. On this page you'll also see Export Private Key. Never share your private key with anyone. Like your 12 words, it opens your wallet. Now the second backup, on paper. Tap Backup, then Back up manually. Read these three: losing your mnemonic phrase means losing your assets for good. Deleting the app deletes the wallet data. And back up somewhere private, with no person and no camera around you. Tick them, tap Understood, and enter your 6-digit password. SafePal now shows your 12 words, and it hides this screen from recordings, to protect you. Write the 12 words on paper, in order, and keep them offline. Never take a screenshot, never copy them, never store them online, and never send them to anyone. Then tap Next, and tap the words in the same order, to prove you wrote them down correctly. Made a mistake? Clear them and try again. When they're right, tap Verify. Backup completed. Two green ticks: Google Drive, and manual. Well done. Most people skip this part, and you didn't. Now, clean up your wallet. You only need three coins. Now let's clean up your wallet, so it shows only what Bitcoin Wealth needs. On the wallet home, tap the three dots next to Search, then Manage Coins. Turn off every coin except BNB, BEP20. BNB pays the small network fees, called gas. Tap the plus, search USDT, and turn on USDT, BEP20. BEP20 means it runs on BNB Smart Chain, Binance's blockchain. Then search BTC, and turn on BTCB, BEP20. BTCB is Bitcoin's value on BNB Smart Chain. It follows the price of Bitcoin one to one, and it's what Bitcoin Wealth runs on. Back on the wallet home, you should see just three coins: BNB, BTCB and USDT. If yours looks like mine, comment DONE. Builders, a website like this one, with your own name and your links, does the explaining for you. BW stands for Bitcoin Wealth, and you can order yours at mtgtribe.com/bwcopy. So, what does it cost to start? So what does it cost to get started? I checked on CoinGecko on 14 November 2026. Bitcoin was about $67,200. The minimum to start Bitcoin Wealth is 0.001 Bitcoin, 1 thousandth of a Bitcoin. That was about $67. And the 0.001 is a once-off. You never pay again to move up to the next slots. That day, $1 was about R16.98. I'd prepare about $76, around R1,300. That covers the 0.001, the fees from your bank to VALR, and from VALR to SafePal, and a little BNB for gas. No VALR or Binance account yet? Tap the buttons below this video to open one. I use both. It's smart to have a backup, just like having more than one income stream. Prices change every day. The entry is fixed in Bitcoin, so when Bitcoin is lower, you need fewer rands to start, and when it's higher, you need more. Ready to join? If I invited you, go to mtgtribe.com/bw. If someone else invited you, use their link, so you join their team. We meet live on Zoom 5 evenings a week, in 4 languages. Ask the person who invited you to add you to the WhatsApp group, or tap the WhatsApp button below this video. Let's recap what we covered in this video. We downloaded the official SafePal app. We created a brand new wallet. We backed it up two ways, on Google Drive and on paper. And we cleaned it up to show BNB, BTCB and USDT. In the next video, part 2, I'll show you how to fund your SafePal wallet with BNB, and swap it for BTCB, ready for Bitcoin Wealth. And remember: everyone needs their own copy. mtgtribe.com/bwcopy. This video is for every team, so feel free to share it. Save this video, so it's here when you need it. Share it with someone who's ready to start. We learn best when we teach others. It pays to pay attention, and take action. Quick reminder: none of this is financial advice. Always do your own research. Thank you for tuning in, and for every like, share, and comment. Your support means everything. And thank yourself for taking massive action today to change your future! I wish you nothing but the best, because YOU are the best. I'm MTG, Your Digital Architect. See you on the next one. Let's Get This Crypto! 💪","hasPart":[{"@type":"Clip","name":"Download the official SafePal app","startOffset":44,"endOffset":114,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=44"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Back up your wallet, two ways","startOffset":114,"endOffset":239,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=114"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"Clean up your wallet","startOffset":239,"endOffset":304,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=239"},{"@type":"Clip","name":"What it costs to start","startOffset":304,"endOffset":379,"url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=304"}],"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#video-t1","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#webpage"}},{"@type":"HowTo","name":"How to set up your SafePal wallet for Bitcoin Wealth","description":"Download SafePal from the official site, create a wallet, back it up two ways, and keep only BNB, USDT and BTCB.","inLanguage":"en-ZA","totalTime":"PT7M25S","video":{"@id":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/#video-t1"},"step":[{"@type":"HowToSection","name":"Download the official SafePal app","position":1,"itemListElement":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Go to safepal.com","text":"Open your browser and go to safepal.com, the official website. Always download apps from the official website, never from a link someone sends you. Scroll down, and tap Download App.","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=51"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Get it on Google Play","text":"On Android, tap Get it on Google Play. On iPhone, tap App Store.","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=62"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Check it, then Install","text":"Before you install, check two things: the developer, SafePal Wallet, and more than 5 million downloads. That's how you know it's the real app. Then tap Install.","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=67"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Decline offer, then Open","text":"If Google Play shows you an offer, tap Decline offer. Stay focused. When it's done, tap Open.","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safepal-wallet-setup/?t=77"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":5,"name":"Create New Wallet","text":"Tap Create New Wallet. We're making a brand new wallet, just for Bitcoin Wealth.","url":"https://mtgtribe.com/bw/dashboard/tutorials/safep