ade at 24 times its size, like paying for one market stall and trading the size of 24. $50 becomes $1,200 and $200 becomes $4,800, which is $6,000 of exposure. Exposure is the size you trade with, not money you own, the loss limit is written down, and you can try your own numbers in the Exposure Calculator.","thumbnailUrl":"https://mtgtribe.com/jetup/img/cover-explainer-amplify-24x-v2.jpg","uploadDate":"2026-11-06T00:00:00+02:00","duration":"PT2M13S","contentUrl":"https://mtgtribe.com/jetup/media/jetup-explainer-amplify-24x-v2.mp4","inLanguage":"en-ZA"}]}</script>
